 "text": "Hello! How's everything today? Most people clean them once or twice a year, usually after painting. Do you know how? That's likely part of it. Brush hairs absorb moisture, then expand, and push the bristles out of the slot. Mostly yes, but some are best discarded. Pull out the damaged ones and cut the soft ones down to about a third. Then just buy new ones. A set of good brushes is cheap compared to how much paint you use.",
